On Sunday afternoon, I take Tommy for a long walk.
I also have his little rubber ball in my hand.
We reach a quiet grassy field.
I throw the ball a short distance.
I say to him: "Tommy, go and catch the ball!"
With great delight, he runs and catches the ball.
I call out: "Now bring it here!"
Tommy runs to me, and I pet him.
He likes this game very much.
Ahead on the path, there is a big muddy puddle.
He slowly walks towards it.
He must not go into that water.
I call out loudly: "Tommy, stop!"
"Do not go there, come here immediately!"
Tommy stops and looks at me.
I say strictly: "You must not go into that water."
"You absolutely must stay with me."
He comes back to me without going into the mud.
I pet him again, and then we continue walking.
